hrough the hose into the bag."},{"role":"name","text":"This is an air suspension."},{"role":"fact","text":"The gauge beside the tank climbs until it reaches 150 psi, and the tank holds air at 100 to 150 psi."},{"role":"factProof","text":"At 100 psi, a bag about six inches across pushes up on the order of 2800 pounds."},{"role":"finish","text":"Add a pressure gauge and a switch box, so you set the ride height yourself."},{"role":"congrats","text":"Congratulations, you have built an air suspension."}]}